  "text": "GenStone Project Highlights – April 2026 Exterior Upgrades & Entryway Projects\n\nAmanda Lombard\nDirector\n\nApril marks the start of exterior project season, with homeowners focusing on curb appeal and front-of-home upgrades. This month’s projects highlight entryways, facades, and outdoor improvements that create a more finished, inviting look. These upgrades show how GenStone can quickly elevate the appearance of a home without the complexity of traditional masonry.\nTry Visualizer Get Project Planning Guide\n\n“I absolutely love the way GenStone looks on my house. It really upgraded the exterior and made everything feel more complete.”\n\nLisa\n\nExterior Facade Projects\n\nExplore stone siding ideas\n\nExterior upgrades are one of the most impactful ways to improve curb appeal, especially as spring projects get underway. This month featured projects where homeowners added stone to front elevations, siding transitions, and visible exterior surfaces. These upgrades add depth, texture, and a more architectural look that makes the entire home feel more complete.\n\n3728\n\nGarry’s Home Siding Transformation\nFaux stone offers a simple and affordable option for a DIY home siding transformation. Take a look at Garry's project!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/mqH9kpxw8v83vKQg28H7U9.jpg\" data-uuid=\"mqH9kpxw8v83vKQg28H7U9\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 2957\n\nHow Earl Covered His Old Brick Wall\nYou can cover up an old brick wall with GenStone faux stone panels. Watch how Earl, a 79 year old weekend warrior covered up his old brick.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\n1757\n\nTom’s DIY Home Siding Transformation\nGenStone is perfect for a DIY home siding transformation like this customer did. Take a look at their stunning before and after photos!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\nKevin O'Dwyer\nGeneral Manager\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/bdh71L1Z1x6mvswBvLR7tZ.jpg\" data-uuid=\"bdh71L1Z1x6mvswBvLR7tZ\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 268\n\nNew Siding for Doug’s Home\nSee how Doug transformed the outside of his home using our stacked stone siding! For fireplace finish ideas, browse GenStone's home siding options today!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\n175\n\nDoctor’s Office in Virginia\nThis Virginia doctor's office used our faux brick veneer to make the building stand out. GenStone's DIY options made this project easy!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nMulti Color\n\n143\n\nPaul’s Faux Stone Home Siding\nNorthern Slate faux stone transformed this customer's home siding and front door columns, complementing the home and making it unique.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/Nq8bPwc2kQXKQ2LJZ5vknK.jpg\" data-uuid=\"Nq8bPwc2kQXKQ2LJZ5vknK\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 104\n\nStacked Stone Siding, Before and After\nGenStone Stratford Stacked Stone panels complete a beautiful exterior siding remodel. See before and after photos.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\n93\n\nJohn’s Faux Stone Garage Siding and Front Door\nGenStone's faux stone offers a full siding solution, so you can enhance your garage and front door in a simple DIY project.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n92\n\nFaux Stone Home Siding Remodel\nThis huge faux stone home siding remodel project shows that GenStone is great for large applications. Check out the before and after photos!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\nZach Erhardt\nManager\n\n83\n\nBrian’s Faux Stone Bay Window Trim\nThis customer used faux stone for trim around their home's bay window. It's the perfect DIY project to add character to the home exterior.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n72\n\nFaux Stone Assisted Living Facility\nNo project is too big! Take a look at this faux stone assisted living facility transformation using stacked stone panels, columns & skirting.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\nRyan Walsh\nProject Coordinator\n\n57\n\nDan’s Stone Veneer Garage Front\nThis customer opted for Keystone Stacked Stone to put stone veneer around his garage front to make it stand out and be more inviting.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n47\n\nAngie’s Faux Stone Stair Risers\nThis customer completed a huge transformation with our faux stone, including stair risers, pillars for the porch and patio, under their bay window, and garage wainscoting. Check it out!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\n45\n\nBarbara’s Stone Veneer Home Siding Project\nIf you want to update your home siding, you can do it as a DIY project using our faux stone. Take a look at Barbara's project for inspiration!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n45\n\nRyan’s DIY Porch Siding Replacement\nThis DIY porch siding replacement brought this porch to life and added depth the old vinyl siding did not offer. Take a look!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\nFront Door & Entryway Projects\n\nView more front door and entry ideas\n\nEntryways are one of the first things people notice about a home, making them a natural focus for spring upgrades. April projects included front door surrounds and entry facades that created a more welcoming, finished appearance. These improvements are a simple way to make a strong first impression while tying together the rest of the exterior.\n\n1193\n\nStephanie’s Stacked Stone Front Entry\nBeautiful entryway that frames the doors and gives a stark contrast to the paint and wood of the rest of the exterior.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nIron Ore\n\nEllie Peretz\nAssistant Manager\n\n239\n\nLuke’s Faux Stone Front Door Siding\nOur faux stone is great for homes and businesses, like this front door siding project. Take a look at Luke's new front door siding!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\n93\n\nJohn’s Faux Stone Garage Siding and Front Door\nGenStone's faux stone offers a full siding solution, so you can enhance your garage and front door in a simple DIY project.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n49\n\nRichard’s DIY Stone Veneer Front Door & Porch Pillars\nOur stone veneer is perfect for a DIY transformation of your front door and porch pillars. Take a look at Richard's project!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nVanilla Bean\n\nEllie Peretz\nAssistant Manager\n\n48\n\nSteve’s Metal Home Wainscot\nDIY Metal Home Wainscot Project By Steve, upgrade the exterior walls of your home with a faux stone wainscot by GenStone.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n43\n\nMike’s DIY Front Door and Garage Wainscoting\nStone veneer is perfect for a home DIY project around your front door and as garage wainscoting. Take a look at this project!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\nKyle Reichrath\nProject Coordinator\n\n38\n\nHome Siding Makeover\nThis home and garage siding makeover project transformed the front of this customer's home with the aesthetic of natural stone.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n36\n\nFaux Stone Porch Walls Design\nThis project upgraded and transformed these porch walls and porch wall siding with faux stone, making the entryway stand out!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n35\n\nDIY Siding Remodel Project Before and After\nStratford Stacked Stone transformed this home exterior siding in a DIY remodel project. Check out the before and after photos!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\n32\n\nPhil’s Wainscoting and Front Door Facelift\nOur faux stone is the DIY solution to remodel your front door. Check out the before and after on this wainscoting and front door facelift!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n25\n\nAnthony’s Stacked Stone DIY Front Door\nLooking for inspiration to remodel your front door? Stacked Stone is the perfect choice for a DIY project on your front door!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n22\n\nHarry’s Stone Veneer DIY Exterior Wainscoting\nStone veneer is the perfect DIY home exterior solution for a wainscoting or front door project like this one. Check it out!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n21\n\nJoe’s Patio Accent Wall\nJoe used GenStone's bright Vanilla Bean panels to create a stunning patio accent wall and entrance!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nVanilla Bean\n\nRob Dean\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\n17\n\nMarc’s Faux Stone Wainscoting on a Metal Building\nYou can install faux stone on anything, like this wainscoting project on a metal building. Take a look at this front door wainscoting!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n16\n\nLeif’s Rock Siding Design\nFor unique exterior home design ideas & garage siding options, see how GenStone's faux stone panels improved the look of Leif's garage & entry rock siding!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\nWhat Our Customers Are Saying\n\n“GenStone completely changed the look of the front of my house. It made a huge difference in curb appeal and gave it a much more finished appearance.”\n\n“We used GenStone outside and it made a huge difference. The space looks more complete and much more like an outdoor living area now.”\n\n“We used GenStone on our front entryway and couldn’t believe how fast it came together. It looks like real stone and really improved the overall look.”\n\nFAQs\nAsk Away. We've Heard it All.\n\nAre GenStone panels weather resistant?\n\nYes. GenStone panels are designed to withstand outdoor conditions including rain, snow, and temperature changes, making them suitable for exterior projects.\n\nAmanda Lombard\n\nDirector\n\nCan GenStone be installed indoors and outdoors?\n\nYes. GenStone panels are designed for both interior and exterior applications. They are commonly used for accent walls, fireplace surrounds, entryways, garages, outdoor kitchens, and exterior facades.\n\nEvan Trevenna\n\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\nHow do I estimate how much GenStone I need for my project?\n\nYou can use the GenStone material calculator or contact a Project Coordinator for a full estimate. Most homeowners measure the square footage of the wall area and then account for corners, trim, and a small 5% waste factor.\n\nTravis Choate\n\nProject Coordinator\n\nDo GenStone panels require maintenance?\n\nGenStone requires very little maintenance. Most installations only need occasional cleaning with mild soap and water to remove dust or debris.\n\nJagger Gottschalk\n\nProject Coordinator\n\nTrending Upgrade Areas this Month\n\nAccent Wall Projects\n\nCreate a bold focal point in any room with lightweight stone panels that install quickly and add depth, texture, and warmth.\n\nView Projects\n\nFireplace Stone Projects\n\nTurn your fireplace into a stunning centerpiece with stacked stone panels that create a warm, modern, or rustic focal point.\n\nView Projects\n\nPorch & Column Upgrades\n\nWrap porch columns or half walls with stone to create a more substantial, finished look that enhances your home’s exterior style.\r\n\nView Projects",
